\begin_layout Standard
We round up our results by proving that for packing spheres in any constant
 dimension 
\begin_inset Formula $d$
\end_inset

, there is a polynomial time 3-approximation algorithm that outputs a solution
 using only rational coordinates.
 For any dimension 
\begin_inset Formula $d\le8$
\end_inset

 our approximation ratio improves even to 
\begin_inset Formula $2+\epsilon$
\end_inset

.
 In particular, this implies that requiring rational coordiantes for the
 computed spheres costs at most a factor of 3 and 
\begin_inset Formula $2+\epsilon$
\end_inset

 in the objective, respectively.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We leave it as an open question to determine whether irrational coordinates
 are sometimes necessary in optimal solutions for geometric knapsack for
