 If yes, it would be interesting to determine the best possible approximation
 ratio one can achieve with rational coordinates only.
 Note that this question is related to the well-studied problem of determining
 the size of the smallest knapsack that is needed to pack a given number
 of unit circles [?].
 For that problem, it is known that for some number of unit circles the
 smallest knapsack has irrational edge lengths
