\begin_layout Standard
Our first result (Theorem
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset

) shows that, for the geometric knapsack problem with 
\begin_inset Formula $d$
\end_inset

-dimensional hyperspheres, there is a polynomial time algorithm that computes
 a set of hyperspheres with profit at least 
\begin_inset Formula $(1-\varepsilon)$
